                <pb facs="0464" n="452" sameAs="frus:frus1942v05/pg452"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">835.796/309: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Armour</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-11-06T00:00:00-04:00">November 6,
                        1942—midnight</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1677. Your 2140, October 31, 5 p.m. You are authorized to inform Intava that
                    there will be no objection to supplying Condor, on a spot delivery basis, and
                    until further notice, reasonable quantities of fuel as required for individual
                    flights for the Buenos Aires–Rio service. Condor should not be allowed to
                    accumulate any excess stocks, and a careful record should be kept of deliveries
                    under this authorization.</p>
                <p>(Repeated to Rio de Janeiro.)</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
